A||||1||Dan86gt3.8||anyone know where the fan relay is?||||1||
Z||000000||Dan86gt3.8||09-03-2000||05:26 AM||||Ok I had a cooling fan that was not working.  We put in a different fan that works.  But it was loose and was scraping the radiator and making all kinda racket.  So I took it out and tightended that nut that holds the blade to the electric motor.  I plugged it back in and the fan does not turn on.  It always used to turn on right when I turned on the ignition.  I also turned on the ac and that did not make it come on.  Which leads me to believe that the relay is bad.  Which leads me to the next question where the heck is it?  The chiltons manual talks about a "fuseable link" and this relay but they left out the part about where the hell in the car it is!  Anywho if you have and ideas comnets or concerns please respond, especially if you know where that damn relay is.<P>ps we hooked the fan up to a battery and it spun like crazy so its not the fan its in the switches somewheres<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>15" konig monsoon's<BR>rear swaybar/ and urethane on rear.<BR>Soon to come urethane all the way around. and new yellow paint w/ raised spoiler!!!!<BR>(also in way future years forced induction on my 3.8!!!!!!!!!)||||reg||1
Z||000001||hugh||09-03-2000||08:05 AM||||I have an 88GT,if they are the same it is under the headlight on the drivers side.When I got my car the relay was eliminated and I played hell trying to find it.Someone had jumped from the control wire directly to the fan supply wire and eliminated the relay altogether(not good)You may have the same condition since your fan always comes on when you turn on the ignition,or the wire that controls the relay is grounded all the time because of a bad temperature switch on your engine,or has been hooked to ground by someone.If you get a 12 volt test light and find the relay,with the key off you should have one wire electrically hot,with the key on there should be 3 wires hot the original(which is one of the larger wires),another large wire which should go to the fan motor,and a smaller wire that is the relay coil wire.If only the smaller wire gets hot,along with the first big wire,then the relay is bad.I hope this understandable and not too long.Good luck.||||reg||1
